WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.635
-Our next guest
is a very funny comedian

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.037
and correspondent
on "The Daily Show."

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.105
His stand-up special
"Imperfect Messenger"

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.341
premieres Friday on
Comedy Central at 10:30.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.775
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:13.413
-You ever been somewhere and
there's too many American flags?

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.748
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:18.151
It just feels...

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.353
There's a little too much
freedom in this space.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.221
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:23.656
And it just don't feel right.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:28.695
Like, how many American flags
equal one Confederate flag?

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:32.231
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Roy Wood Jr.!

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:34.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:40.373 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:46.145 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.181
-Yes.
-Hi. Welcome back.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.582
-They look good.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.584
-It has --
-What's happening, man?

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.486
-It has been a minute
since you've been here.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.121
2014 was the last time
you were here.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.056
-Yeah, man. I came in here
and did the damn thing

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:59.392
and then got "The Daily Show"
like not too long after that.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.227
-That's right. Then
you were a very busy man.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.062
And I'm happy when you're busy.
I'm a huge fan of your work.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.330
I love seeing you
on "The Daily Show."

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.698
I love seeing your stand-up.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.534
-Man, I love seeing you,
as well.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.837
I was trying to come see you
in Boston.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.171
You was doing the live show.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:13.906
-Yep. July.
-In Boston.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.174
And I was in Boston.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:16.676
We were shooting "Confess,
Fletch" with Jon Hamm.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.111
We was wrapping up production
on "Fletch."

00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:22.281
And then the more I wanted to
come there, the more I realized

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:23.849
I don't, like --
You know how like --

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:25.652
There's a lot of wrong ways
to catch COVID.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:29.121
You don't want to catch COVID
going to the Seth Meyers show...

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:31.390
and then bring it back
to Jon Hamm.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.360
-No.
-That's a terrible situation.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.795
And then also your fans --

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.430
Here's the thing
I also noticed about --

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.298
Like, your fans, there's
a little bit of overlap

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:41.066
between the people who love you
and who love "The Daily Show."

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:43.736
-Yes, sir.
-And these people talk a lot.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.138
And they mean well,
but it's COVID.

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:47.940
I need you to keep it short.
-Yep.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.409
-But the people, they're like,

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.510
[Throaty]
"Hey, I just want you to know

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.980
how much you mean to me.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:56.849
Just -- I love you."

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:59.886
I'm like, "Hey,
I would rather you hate me

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.587
'cause it's a quicker
conversation."

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:03.255
-Right, because if you run
into somebody who hates you,

00:02:03.255 --> 00:02:04.590
it's much quicker, yeah.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.293
-"Hey, hey, hey! Kiss my ass!"
I'm like, "Thank you."

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.061
-[ Laughter ]
-That was brief.

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:11.898
That was a brief conversation.
-Did you ever catch COVID?

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:15.735
-Yeah, but, see, I caught it --
I caught COVID in the early days

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.536
when you still had to
be ashamed about it.

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:19.371
-Uh-huh.

00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:20.907
-You remember the early days
of COVID.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:25.245
"I just want y'all to know
I'm doing fine and we are --

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:28.314
we are taking
all the precautions."

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:33.686
Like, you had to whisper,
"I had it, but then I..."

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.554
You catch COVID now,
you can tell everybody.

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:38.590
"Yeah, bitch, I had it.
I had it three times! What?

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.826
Hey, I caught COVID.
I'm going to the grocery store.

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:42.161
You want something?"

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:44.163
-I would love it, yeah.
You got the antibodies. Go.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:45.798
-Yeah, people are wide open
with it now.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.132
I had the whisper COVID.
-Yeah.

00:02:47.132 --> 00:02:48.868
Oh, the whisper COVID.
That was the worst one to get.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.604
Everybody says Delta is bad.
Whisper, that's the tough one.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:52.772
-That's the one.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.173
-That's the one
you don't want to get.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:56.175
We were talking backstage.
I'm so impressed by this.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.110
Because I was watching
your special

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.845
and I was thinking to myself,
"Gosh, this feels really fresh

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.981
and of the moment."

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.916
And a lot of times --
People don't know this --

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:06.352
But specials are shot
four, six, eight months

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.686
before people can see them.

00:03:07.686 --> 00:03:09.556
You shot this two weeks ago.
-Shot it two weeks ago.

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:11.124
-That's amazing.
-Shot it two weeks ago.

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.624
-And you can tell,
and it's wonderful

00:03:12.624 --> 00:03:14.527
to see something
that's this new.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.695
-The world changes too fast,

00:03:16.695 --> 00:03:19.265
and the last thing I want to be
is the comedian with a special

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:22.301
that's not on the pulse of
where we are as a people now.

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:26.072
Comedy when it's at its best is
on the finger of the pulse now,

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:28.340
not what was three, four,
five, six months ago.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.676
So, you know, I'm very thankful
to Comedy Central

00:03:30.676 --> 00:03:33.446
and the production team for,
you know, being able to help me

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.748
turn it around that fast,
'cause that's what I wanted.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:38.718
Like, you don't want to be
the dude talking about Delta

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.753
in your special
and we done moved on

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:43.656
to Omega, Lambda, Sigma, Theta.
-Yeah.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.892
-So, you know --
-I mean, if you did a special

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.093
six months ago, you very
possibly could have like,

00:03:48.093 --> 00:03:49.862
"It's over!"
-Yeah.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.830
-Then people would be watching
it now and be like,

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.299
"Where was he?"

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.301
-Yeah, or the asteroid
could hit. You never know.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.002
-Right.
-Anything could happen.

00:03:57.002 --> 00:03:59.138
-That would be the worst thing
about an asteroid hitting,

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:00.940
would be your special
not being timely.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.007
-Yes.

00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:03.643
-You talk about police
in your special.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.444
You know, law enforcement.
You also mention

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:08.180
you have a couple of family
members in law enforcement.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.951
-So, I mean, Thanksgiving
should be okay.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.720
I don't really go in
on the police.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.254
I was trying to, like, you know,

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:18.891
just present different prisms
into police reform.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.759
For sure,
I know one of my cousins,

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:22.328
he ain't gonna be offended

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:25.765
'cause he is one of the laziest
state troopers.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:28.267
Which honestly is just like

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:31.304
a beautiful bridge
to help with the community.

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:33.272
It's -- You ever feel good
when you see somebody

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:35.674
not be good at they job?
-Yeah.

00:04:35.674 --> 00:04:37.076
-I'll be like, "All right, man,

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.645
maybe you are one
of the good ones.

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.813
You didn't even
tuck in your shirt."

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:44.917
He drives his squad car
on his off days.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.220
-In uniform or out?
-No. Regular clothes.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:50.356
Like, he drives a police car
in regular clothes,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.791
then wants me to go run errands
with him.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.359
I'm like, "First off,
you need to take the car

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:56.729
back to the station. It ain't
supposed to be at your house."

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.998
And he like, "I'm just running
to Dollar Tree right quick.

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.399
Come with me."

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.668
I'm like, "No, bitch.
I'm not riding with you."

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:05.904
In a squad -- Two black dudes in
regular clothes in a police car?

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:08.441
This --
Do the other police know?

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.776
"Man, they know me."
I'm like, "No."

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:12.845
"All right, well,
I'm gonna go change.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.247
I'm gonna go put on my uniform."

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.648
I'm like,
"That don't solve my problem."

00:05:16.648 --> 00:05:18.918
You in uniform.
I'm sitting up front with you.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:21.187
I'm wearing regular clothes.
Now I look like a snitch.

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.122
I look like --

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:25.224
Look like you taking me
to Dollar Tree

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.226
to reward me for snitching.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:29.662
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.497
So...
-I get it, man.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:35.735
-I love him. I love him, man.
-I love seeing you.

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:37.636
I love the special.
It's really something else.

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:39.405
Thanks so much for
making time for us, Roy.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.440
It is always such a pleasure.
-Thank you for having me, man.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.375
-You guys, that's Roy Wood Jr.

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:44.843
"Imperfect Messenger"

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:47.080
premieres Friday on
Comedy Central at 10:30.

